STATUS: paper.pdf not obtained during 2026-07-05 8-artifact backfill (90s fetch cap).

DOI: 10.3390/antibiotics12101519
PMID: 37887221
PMC: PMC10604428
Open access: CC BY 4.0 (MDPI GOLD OA per Unpaywall + Semantic Scholar)

Fetch attempts (all within 90s cap, all failed):
1. https://www.mdpi.com/2079-6382/12/10/1519/pdf                       → HTTP 200 "Access Denied" (Akamai anti-bot)
2. https://europepmc.org/backend/ptpmcrender.fcgi?accid=PMC10604428... → curl STREAM_CLOSED (HTTP/2 err 5)
3. https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10604428/pdf/antib...  → JS interstitial (cloudpmc-viewer)
4. https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10604428/pdf/antibioti...   → JS interstitial (cloudpmc-viewer)
5. Cookied requests with Referer=Scholar / Referer=article page       → still Access Denied on MDPI
6. Version-pinned Unpaywall URL                                        → Access Denied

Root cause: both MDPI (Akamai + JS challenge) and NCBI PMC (JavaScript interstitial for PDF endpoint,
requires cloudpmc-viewer JS to resolve to actual PDF) block unattended curl. Full JATS XML full text
IS available (already pulled to work/paper_pmc.xml, 124 KB) so the entire paper content is present
in this replication dir — just not as a PDF blob.

To close:
- Use headless browser (Playwright) with real UA + cookies to bypass MDPI Akamai.
- Or resolve via institutional proxy (ANL library, UChicago) which whitelists MDPI PDFs.
- Or run from a machine with a persistent NCBI PMC JS session and fetch through the resolved URL.

Note: `work/paper_text.md` (26.8 KB, plain-text extraction of the JATS XML) IS a complete
full-text extraction of the paper and is used as the ground truth for re-reading and open-question
generation. `extraction/marker.md` (item 2 of the standard) is derived from this JATS XML extraction
rather than from a Marker parse of paper.pdf; this is documented in `extraction/marker.md` header.
